        "original_id": "6a84d64a-2ba4-56a1-b634-3fe470177aeb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sharon Gless, Ron Cowen, Daniel Lipman, Tony Jonas, Robert Fuest, David Wiltse, Peter Maloney, Julie Kavner, Don Johnson, Arthur Hill, Audra Lindley\n- Products: Switch, Cagney & Lacey, The Trials of Rosie O'Neill, Queer as Folk, Burn Notice, Revenge of the Stepford Wives, The Knick, Remember WENN, Gotham, Greetings, Capone, A Little Romance, Hide in Plain Sight, The Children, The Thing, Desperately Seeking Susan, Manhunter, Tune in Tomorrow, JFK, Private Parts, Boiler Room, Requiem for a Dream, K-PAX\n- Roles: Maggie Philbin, Sgt. Christine Cagney, Debbie Novotny, Madeline Westen\n- Companies: Warner Bros.\n\nFacts:\n- Sharon Gless was born on May 31, 1943, and she is an American actress of stage, film, and television.\n- Sharon Gless played Maggie Philbin on Switch from 1975 to 1978.\n- Peter Maloney appeared in the film Greetings in 1968.\n- Peter Maloney appeared in the film Capone in 1975.\n- Peter Maloney appeared in the film A Little Romance in 1979.\n- In 1980, Revenge of the Stepford Wives was directed by Robert Fuest and written by David Wiltse.\n- In 1980, Revenge of the Stepford Wives starred Sharon Gless, Julie Kavner, Don Johnson, Arthur Hill, and Audra Lindley.\n- Peter Maloney appeared in the films Hide in Plain Sight, The Children, and Revenge of the Stepford Wives in 1980.\n- Sharon Gless played Sgt. Christine Cagney in Cagney & Lacey from 1982 to 1988.\n- Peter Maloney appeared in the film The Thing in 1982 and in Desperately Seeking Susan in 1985.\n- Peter Maloney appeared in the film Manhunter in 1986.\n- Sharon Gless played the title role in The Trials of Rosie O'Neill from 1990 to 1992.\n- Peter Maloney appeared in Tune in Tomorrow in 1990, JFK in 1991, Private Parts in 1997, Boiler Room in 2000, Requiem for a Dream in 2000, and K-PAX in 2001.\n- Ron Cowen and Daniel Lipman developed and wrote the U.S. television series Queer as Folk, and they served as its showrunners.\n- Ron Cowen, Daniel Lipman, and Tony Jonas, a former president of Warner Bros., served as executive producers of Queer as Folk.\n- Sharon Gless played Debbie Novotny in the Showtime series Queer as Folk from 2000 to 2005.\n- Sharon Gless played Madeline Westen on Burn Notice from 2007 to 2013.\n- Peter Maloney's television credits include The Knick, Remember WENN, and Gotham.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
